tatus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BANDO CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, KATUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA KATUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, KATUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A transmission belt comprising a compression rubber layer and an adhesion rubber layer, which have been subjected to vulcanization adhesion to each other, and, buried in the adhesion rubber layer, a reinforcement comprising a polyester fiber, characterized in that both of the compression rubber layer and the adhesion rubber layer comprise an ethylene- alpha -olefin-diene rubber and the reinforcement is buried in the adhesion rubber layer after having been subjected to an adhesion treatment with a resorcin-formalin-latex adhesive composition, wherein 50 to 100 wt % of solids in the resorcin-formalin-latex adhesive composition consists of at least one selected from chlorosulfonated polyethylene and an alkylated chlorosulfonated polyethylene; and a method for manufacturing the transmission belt with good productivity.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une courroie de transmission comprenant une couche caoutchouc de compression et une couche caoutchouc adhésive, collées l'une à l'autre par vulcanisation et, planté dans la couche adhésive, un renforcement en fibres polyester. Ladite courroie se caractérise en ce que la couche caoutchouc de compression et la couche caoutchouc adhésive sont en caoutchouc  alpha -oléfine-diène d'éthylène et le renforcement est planté dans la couche caoutchouc adhésive après avoir subi un traitement d'adhésion au moyen d'une composition adhésive au latex-formaline-résorcine, dans laquelle 50 à 100 % en poids de solides sont au moins un choisi dans du polyéthylène chlorosulfoné et un polyéthylène chlorosulfoné alkylé. L'invention concerne enfin un procédé de fabrication d'une courroie de transmission présentant une bonne productivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>